. [Java/Kotlin Lists](../evidence/jvm-lists-20260920.md) use primitive or reference arrays, with independently compiled consumers and runtime-only deployment on both paths. [Ruby Lists](../evidence/ruby-lists-20260921.md) use copied Arrays, with installed checks and relocated gem execution on both paths. [Perl Lists](../evidence/perl-lists-20260921.md) use plain array references, with installed checks on both source paths and all four pinned Perl ABIs. [Native PHP Lists](../evidence/php-native-lists-20260921.md) use consecutive-key arrays, with installed weak/strict checks on both source paths. [PHP-Wasm Lists](../evidence/php-wasm-lists-20260921.md) use consecutive-key arrays with 32-bit PHP mappings, with installed Node/Chromium checks on both source paths. [WIT/WASI Lists](../evidence/wit-lists-20260921.md) use canonical lists through the packaged Wasmtime host, with installed checks on both source paths. Copied Lists and transparent aliases now cover all seventeen consumer profiles, including [WIT/WASI aliases](../evidence/wit-aliases-20260921.md). Concrete, non-recursive tagged variants have installed checks in all five [npm profiles](../evidence/npm-variants-20260921.md), [C++](../evidence/cpp-variants-20260921.md), [C/C-GMP](../evidence/c-variants-20260921.md), [Python](../evidence/python-variants-20260921.md), [Rust](../evidence/rust-variants-20260921.md), [C#](../evidence/dotnet-variants-20260921.md), [Java/Kotlin](../evidence/jvm-variants-20260921.md), [Ruby](../evidence/ruby-variants-20260921.md), [Perl](../evidence/perl-variants-20260921.md), [native PHP](../evidence/php-native-variants-20260921.md), [PHP-Wasm](../evidence/php-wasm-variants-20260921.md) and [WIT/WASI](../evidence/wit-variants-20260921.md). [Recursive npm values](../evidence/npm-recursive-20260922.md) have installed checks on both source paths across all five npm profiles, including Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. [Recursive C/C++ packages](../evidence/native-recursive-packages-20260923.md) also pass installed checks on both source paths, including source-free deployment. [Recursive Rust packages](../evidence/rust-recursive-packages-20260923.md), [Python wheels](../evidence/python-recursive-packages-20260923.md), [Ruby gems](../evidence/ruby-recursive-packages-20260923.md) and [Perl CPAN archives](../evidence/perl-recursive-packages-20260923.md) have installed checks on both source paths. Perl covers four pinned ABIs and both prebuilt-only and generated-XS-only installation. [C#, Java, Kotlin, native PHP and PHP-Wasm](../evidence/recursive-managed-acceptance-20260924.md) also pass installed recursive checks on both source paths. [WIT/WASI acceptance](../evidence/wit-recursive-acceptance-20260924.md) completes the copied family. Recursive copied values have installed checks across all seventeen profiles. [Structured C callbacks](../evidence/c-structured-callables-20260924.md), [C++ callbacks](../evidence/cpp-structured-callables-20260924.md), [Rust callbacks](../evidence/rust-structured-callables-20260924.md), [Python callbacks](../evidence/python-structured-callables-20260924.md) and [Ruby callbacks](../evidence/ruby-structured-callables-20260924.md) additionally have installed checks for arrays, Lists, options, results, products, acyclic records, variants and aliases. Recursive callable payloads, structured callables in the other profiles and explicitly owned resource aggregates remain assigned work. Missing mappings and positions remain assigned work in the [type inventory](../type-surface.v1.json)."
